cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "aciR" in publications use:'
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'aciR: Assimilative Causal Inference for Conditional Gaussian Nonlinear Systems'
version: 0.1.0
abstract: Reimplements the assimilative causal inference (ACI) method of Andreou,
  Chen and Bollt (2026) <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-68568-0> for conditional
  Gaussian nonlinear systems (CGNS). Provides the closed-form forward filter and backward
  smoother for the conditional Gaussian statistics of an unobserved component given
  an observed signal, together with the relative-entropy causal-information metric
  that contrasts the smoother posterior against the filter posterior. The numerical
  core is graded against fixtures generated by an independent 'MATLAB' harness reproducing
  the deterministic core of the reference implementation.
